   "title": "State arms agency completes development of homegrown Marine attack helicopter",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/southkorea/defense/20261028/state-arms-agency-completes-development-of-homegrown-marine-attack-helicopter",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Wed, 28 Oct 2026 05:37:03 GMT",
   "_dt": 1793165823.0,
   "ageDays": 0.02,
   "summary": "Korea has completed the development of a homegrown Marine Attack Helicopter (MAH) fitted with a range of weapons systems, including air-to-ground missiles, for multidimensional amphibious operations, the state arms procurement agency said Wednesday.",
   "summary_zh": "韩国国防事业厅周三表示，韩国已完成国产舰载攻击直升机（MAH）的研制，该机配备包括空对地导弹在内的一系列武器系统，可用于多维两栖作战。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Korea has completed the development of a homegrown Marine Attack Helicopter (MAH) fitted with a range of weapons systems, including air-to-ground missiles, for multidimensional amphibious operations, the state arms procurement agency said Wednesday. The attack helicopters are built on a Marine variant of the KUH-1 Surion helicopter, known as the MUH-1 Marineon, with new added features and weapons systems to counter attacks from enemy choppers and drones, according to the Defense Acquisition Program Administration (DAPA). DAPA launched a 450 billion-won ($337 millon) project to develop the homegrown MAH in 2022. Since then, it has completed a number of test flights and weapons tests, including live-fire tests involving turret-mounted machine guns, air-to-ground missiles, and guided and unguided rockets. It passed a full combat suitability evaluation in July and received airworthiness certification in August, guaranteeing the plane's suitability for safe flight. When deployed, the MAH system is expected to expand the Marines' amphibious operations not only on the ground, but also in the air, and serve as a key asset in maximizing the mobility of troops. DAPA said it plans to begin production of some 20 of the helicopters starting next year",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
