   "summary": "Finnish President Alexander Stubb and Norwegian Prime Minister Jonas Gahr Støre have opened a direct line to Vladimir Putin, drawing criticism from some fellow European leaders — even as Ukraine backs their efforts.",
   "summary_zh": "芬兰总统Alexander Stubb和挪威首相Jonas Gahr Støre开通了与Vladimir Putin的直通电话，乌克兰支持两人的努力，但这一做法遭到一些欧洲领导人的批评。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Brussels Playbook Podcast Stories driving the day in Brussels and beyond. Apple Music Amazon Music Europe’s united front on Ukraine is showing cracks. Finnish President Alexander Stubb and Norwegian Prime Minister Jonas Gahr Støre have opened a direct line to Vladimir Putin, drawing criticism from some fellow European leaders — even as Ukraine backs their efforts. Nicholas Vinocur and Paul Dallison examine the fallout and the growing scramble over who gets to speak for Europe in peace talks. Also on the pod: Brussels unveils a sweeping overhaul of Frontex, giving the EU border agency a much bigger role in deportations, new powers to monitor social media and plans for a major expansion. And after a summer of devastating heatwaves and wildfires, the European Commission wants governments to prepare for a world that’s three degrees hotter than preindustrial levels. Finally, you can see the ghostly turnip that freaked Nick out here . And if you have someone spooky in mind for Paul’s story on the figures haunting the EU bubble, please write in! Find us on WhatsApp here or at +32 491 05 06 29",
