   "title": "Farmers call off march to mumbai after fadnavis govt promises drought relief 101793121495093",
   "url": "https://www.hindustantimes.com/india-news/farmers-call-off-march-to-mumbai-after-fadnavis-govt-promises-drought-relief-101793121495093.html",
   "domain": "hindustantimes.com",
   "source": "hindustantimes.com",
   "published": "Tue, 27 Oct 2026 23:04:55 +0530",
   "_dt": 1793122495.0,
   "ageDays": 0.52,
   "summary": "The farmers carrying red flags began their march from Igatpuri to Mumbai along the Nashik–Mumbai highway. In the evening, Fadnavis met a delegation of farmers under the leadership of Ajit Nawale. Maharashtra Chief Minister Devendra Fadnavis has assured farmers that the state government will extend all possible assistance to help them overcome the challenges arising from the prevailing drought conditions.",
   "summary_zh": "举着红旗的农民从伊加特普里出发，沿纳西克—孟买公路向孟买行进。傍晚， Fadnavis会见了由阿吉特·纳瓦莱带领的农民代表团。 Maharashtra首席部长德夫德拉· Fadnavis向农民保证，州政府将提供一切可能的援助，帮助他们克服当前干旱状况带来的挑战。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The farmers carrying red flags began their march from Igatpuri to Mumbai along the Nashik–Mumbai highway. All India Kisan Sabha leader Ajit Nawale called for reform in the farm loan waiver policy. He argued that farmers who regularly repay their loans should benefit from the scheme. In the evening, Fadnavis met a delegation of farmers under the leadership of Ajit Nawale. Maharashtra Chief Minister Devendra Fadnavis has assured farmers that the state government will extend all possible assistance to help them overcome the challenges arising from the prevailing drought conditions. Fadnavis emphasised that the government was committed to reducing the hardships faced by farming families through financial assistance, drinking water arrangements, fodder supplies and measures to strengthen agricultural support systems. The Chief Minister announced that pending instalments under the Namo Shetkari Mahasanman Nidhi Yojana would be paid to eligible farmers. He also assured that the government will consider demand for increasing the ₹ 50,000 incentive provided to farmers who regularly repay their crop loans. \"A ministerial group constituted to examine farm loan waivers will discuss the proposal to increase the incentive. A suitable decision will be taken after considering the state's financial position,\" said Fadnavis. Fadnavis also ordered officials to expedite the release of pending instalments under the Mukhyamantri Majhi Ladki Bahin Yojana for women beneficiaries who have completed their e-KYC verification. The Chief Minister said Maharashtra was among the leading states in terms of the number of women receiving benefits under such welfare schemes. The Chief Minister directed the concerned department to examine the possibility of restoring the triggers previously used under the crop insurance scheme. The state government has expressed a positive view on increasing the monthly honorarium of school nutrition programme workers. These workers currently receive ₹ 2,500 per month, and the proposal under consideration would raise their honorarium by ₹ 1,000 to ₹ 3,500 per month. After the assurance, Ajit Nawale announced the decision to withdraw Long March. \"CM Fadnavis responded positively to our demands. So we have decided to withdraw the Long March.\" said Nawale. The meeting was attended by Deputy Chief Ministers Eknath Shinde and Sunetra Ajit Pawar, Water Resources Minister Radhakrishna Vikhe Patil, Water Resources Minister Girish Mahajan, Revenue Minister Chandrashekhar Bawankule, Agriculture Minister Dattatray Bharne and MLA Vinod Nikole",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "in"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "pol",
    "cor"
   ],
   "tier": 3,
   "actor": "当事国政府",
   "alsoUS": false,
