   "snippet": "TROOPS RESCUE THREE KIDNAPPED VICTIMS IN KEBBI\n\nBy: Zagazola Makama\n\nTroops of the Nigerian Army, in collaboration with other security operatives, have rescued three kidnapped victims during a joint fighting patrol in Sakaba Local Government Area of Kebbi State.\n\nSecurity sources told Zagazola Makama that the operation was conducted at about 10:20 a.m. on Oct. 22 by troops of 223 Battalion, working alongside CT 10 and CIB III, from Dirindaji.\n\nThe sources said the joint team conducted a fighting patrol to Makuku and Dankolo villages, where the three victims were successfully rescued.\n\nFollowing their rescue, the victims were handed over to the District Head of Dirindaji for further action.",
