   "platform": "x",
   "title": "TROOPS ARREST SUSPECTED ISWAP COLLABORATOR OVER FORCED LEVIES IN YOBE By: Zagazola Makama Troops of the Nigerian Army, in collaboration with",
   "url": "https://x.com/ZagazOlaMakama/status/2114480288868823456",
   "snippet": "TROOPS ARREST SUSPECTED ISWAP COLLABORATOR OVER FORCED LEVIES IN YOBE\n\nBy: Zagazola Makama\n\nTroops of the Nigerian Army, in collaboration with the Civilian Joint Task Force (CJTF), have arrested a suspected Islamic State West Africa Province (ISWAP) collaborator at Geidam Market in Geidam Local Government Area of Yobe State.\n\nSecurity sources told Zagazola Makama that the suspect was apprehended at about 1:30 p.m. on Oct. 24 while in possession of a mini truck.\n\nThe sources said preliminary interrogation revealed that the suspect allegedly confessed to actively receiving and delivering proceeds from forced levies imposed on local residents by terrorists.\n\nItems recovered from the suspect included one mobile phone, a lighter and the sum of ₦18,450 in cash.\n\nThe suspect is currently in the custody of the troops for further investigation and necessary action.\n\nThe arrest is significant amid ongoing efforts by security forces to disrupt the financial and logistical networks sustaining terrorist activities in the North-East.\n\nThe collection of forced levies from residents and the subsequent movement of the proceeds are among the methods used by terrorist groups to generate funds and sustain their operations.\n\nSecurity forces continue to intensify intelligence-led operations to identify individuals suspected of facilitating terrorist financing, logistics and other support activities across the region.",
   "body": "TROOPS ARREST SUSPECTED ISWAP COLLABORATOR OVER FORCED LEVIES IN YOBE\n\nBy: Zagazola Makama\n\nTroops of the Nigerian Army, in collaboration with the Civilian Joint Task Force (CJTF), have arrested a suspected Islamic State West Africa Province (ISWAP) collaborator at Geidam Market in Geidam Local Government Area of Yobe State.\n\nSecurity sources told Zagazola Makama that the suspect was apprehended at about 1:30 p.m. on Oct. 24 while in possession of a mini truck.\n\nThe sources said preliminary interrogation revealed that the suspect allegedly confessed to actively receiving and delivering proceeds from forced levies imposed on local residents by terrorists.\n\nItems recovered from the suspect included one mobile phone, a lighter and the sum of ₦18,450 in cash.\n\nThe suspect is currently in the custody of the troops for further investigation and necessary action.\n\nThe arrest is significant amid ongoing efforts by security forces to disrupt the financial and logistical networks sustaining terrorist activities in the North-East.\n\nThe collection of forced levies from residents and the subsequent movement of the proceeds are among the methods used by terrorist groups to generate funds and sustain their operations.\n\nSecurity forces continue to intensify intelligence-led operations to identify individuals suspected of facilitating terrorist financing, logistics and other support activities across the region.",
