   "title": "#BREAKING | 🇩🇿 🇳🇪 — Algeria’s parliament unanimously approved forward deployment of military forces into Niger.",
   "url": "https://x.com/TGEThGlobalEye/status/2114363963735462177",
   "snippet": "#BREAKING | 🇩🇿 🇳🇪 — Algeria’s parliament unanimously approved forward deployment of military forces into Niger. \n\nThis expands Algeria’s presence at Air Base 101 (Niamey International Airport), established after the August 29 attempted coup. Forces will deploy to key oil infrastructure and Madama Air Base (21.9554711, 13.6470986) in the northeast.\n\nAlgeria has softened its stance toward Mali and Burkina Faso while backing the Niamey junta, recently supplying military helicopters. This shift counters the growing influence of Saddam Haftar and eastern Libyan factions, whom Niamey accuses of supporting Tuareg separatists and the anti-junta Patriotic Liberation Front (FPL). Some junta members blame the FPL for the August 29 attacks.\n\nThe deployment positions Algerian forces near FPL operational areas and the Libyan border, specifically Fezzan, which is controlled by remnants of Haftar’s 128th Brigade.",
   "body": "#BREAKING | 🇩🇿 🇳🇪 — Algeria’s parliament unanimously approved forward deployment of military forces into Niger. \n\nThis expands Algeria’s presence at Air Base 101 (Niamey International Airport), established after the August 29 attempted coup. Forces will deploy to key oil infrastructure and Madama Air Base (21.9554711, 13.6470986) in the northeast.\n\nAlgeria has softened its stance toward Mali and Burkina Faso while backing the Niamey junta, recently supplying military helicopters. This shift counters the growing influence of Saddam Haftar and eastern Libyan factions, whom Niamey accuses of supporting Tuareg separatists and the anti-junta Patriotic Liberation Front (FPL). Some junta members blame the FPL for the August 29 attacks.\n\nThe deployment positions Algerian forces near FPL operational areas and the Libyan border, specifically Fezzan, which is controlled by remnants of Haftar’s 128th Brigade.",
