   "title": "1/5 Respectfully, the facts point the other way.",
   "url": "https://x.com/GeoCherifien/status/2114361736316748073",
   "snippet": "1/5\nRespectfully, the facts point the other way. Niger isn't a side issue, it's Algiers' gateway to the whole Sahel. Look at 2026 alone:\n\n🇳🇪 Feb: Tiani in Algiers, ties normalised\n🇳🇪 Aug: Su-30s deployed to Niamey\n🇳🇪 Oct: military protocol, then the Senate approves troops, a first since 1973\n🇳🇪 40 MW power plant gifted, Kafra oil block\n\nSource: Al Jazeera https://t.co/On3gRob3i8\n\n2/5\nAnd Mali? Algiers got back in through Niamey.\n\n🇲🇱 Jul 10: ambassadors back, airspace reopened, a thaw that was mediated by Niger\n🇧🇫 $88M mining & energy package for Burkina\n🇲🇷 Oct 22: Algeria–Mauritania military security meeting in Zouérat\n\nNiger is the door to Bamako, not a detour.\n\nSource: International Crisis Group https://t.co/l6OjcX1aav\n\n3/5\nNow add Ankara 🇹🇷:\n\n• TB2 & Karayel-SU drones in Niger, Turkish instructors on Nigerien bases since April\n• Tiani's first trip outside Africa was to Ankara in June\n• Turkey trained Malian commandos\n\nAlgiers & Ankara set up a strategic council in May, aim for $10B in trade, and share one rival in the region: the UAE.\n\nSource: Turkish Minute https://t.co/3q4NmLZjiY\n\n4/5\nThat's an alliance of convenience, not a bloc, but it works: Turkey sells & trains, Algeria brings troops, gas and money.\n\nOn Russia, I agree it's entrenched. But it's Africa Corps that saved Tiani in August, and Algiers is shoring up Russia's clients, not fighting them. The three are compatible.\n\nSource: Steptoe https://t.co/a4AZBO34GU\n\n5/5\nWhy it matters for Morocco 🇲🇦:\n\n• The Atlantic Initiative needs the AES capitals to want Dakhla\n• Trans-Saharan gas pipeline (via Niger) vs Nigeria–Morocco pipeline\n• Whoever secures Niamey sits on both routes\n\nThe Sahara file is closing. The Sahel file is wide open. Ignoring Niger means handing it over.\n\nSource: ISS Africa",
   "body": "1/5\nRespectfully, the facts point the other way. Niger isn't a side issue, it's Algiers' gateway to the whole Sahel. Look at 2026 alone:\n\n🇳🇪 Feb: Tiani in Algiers, ties normalised\n🇳🇪 Aug: Su-30s deployed to Niamey\n🇳🇪 Oct: military protocol, then the Senate approves troops, a first since 1973\n🇳🇪 40 MW power plant gifted, Kafra oil block\n\nSource: Al Jazeera https://t.co/On3gRob3i8\n\n2/5\nAnd Mali? Algiers got back in through Niamey.\n\n🇲🇱 Jul 10: ambassadors back, airspace reopened, a thaw that was mediated by Niger\n🇧🇫 $88M mining & energy package for Burkina\n🇲🇷 Oct 22: Algeria–Mauritania military security meeting in Zouérat\n\nNiger is the door to Bamako, not a detour.\n\nSource: International Crisis Group https://t.co/l6OjcX1aav\n\n3/5\nNow add Ankara 🇹🇷:\n\n• TB2 & Karayel-SU drones in Niger, Turkish instructors on Nigerien bases since April\n• Tiani's first trip outside Africa was to Ankara in June\n• Turkey trained Malian commandos\n\nAlgiers & Ankara set up a strategic council in May, aim for $10B in trade, and share one rival in the region: the UAE.\n\nSource: Turkish Minute https://t.co/3q4NmLZjiY\n\n4/5\nThat's an alliance of convenience, not a bloc, but it works: Turkey sells & trains, Algeria brings troops, gas and money.\n\nOn Russia, I agree it's entrenched. But it's Africa Corps that saved Tiani in August, and Algiers is shoring up Russia's clients, not fighting them. The three are compatible.\n\nSource: Steptoe https://t.co/a4AZBO34GU\n\n5/5\nWhy it matters for Morocco 🇲🇦:\n\n• The Atlantic Initiative needs the AES capitals to want Dakhla\n• Trans-Saharan gas pipeline (via Niger) vs Nigeria–Morocco pipeline\n• Whoever secures Niamey sits on both routes\n\nThe Sahara file is closing. The Sahel file is wide open. Ignoring Niger means handing it over.\n\nSource: ISS Africa",
